/*
The purpose of the updateDiceAnywhere function is to generate a combined list 
of dice values that are currently in play. This includes dice that the player has 
decided to keep (diceSelected) and dice that have just been rolled and are on 
the table (diceOnTable).

if (diceSelected) { ... }: This checks if there are any dice that the player has 
selected to keep from previous rolls. 
 diceAnywhere = diceOnTable.concat(diceSelected);: If there are selected dice, 
we combine the dice on the table with the selected dice. For example, if 
diceOnTable = [3, 5] and diceSelected = [1, 2, 6], then diceAnywhere will 
become [3, 5, 1, 2, 6]

If there are no selected dice, then the dice that are "anywhere" are simply the 
ones on the table.
*/

function updateDiceAnywhere () {
if (diceSelected) {
diceAnywhere = diceOnTable.concat(diceSelected);
} else {
diceAnywhere = diceOnTable;
}
}

